      "data": {
        "title": "Public Life and Spaceflight Career",
        "body": "Armstrong flew combat missions as a naval aviator, became a research test pilot, and joined NASA’s astronaut corps in 1962. He commanded Gemini VIII, which achieved the first docking of two vehicles in space, and Apollo 11, the first crewed lunar landing. After leaving NASA, he taught aerospace engineering at the University of Cincinnati.",
        "period": "1930–2012",
        "subjectRef": "neil-armstrong",
        "status": "historical",
